{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>יִפְרָח</b> Four times in the Masorah: here, and the others: צַדִּיק כַּתָּמָר יִפְרָח, יִפְרַחְתָּ כַּשׁוֹשַׁנָּה, יִפְרַחַ בְּיָמָיו צַדִּיק. מַטֵּהוּ יִפְרָח — this is צַדִּיק כַּתָּמָר יִפְרָח: since his staff blossomed, the righteous one emerged vindicated in his judgment, and this is יִפְרַחְתָּ כַּשׁוֹשַׁנָּה, and he was like an olive tree flourishing, and this is like the good oil upon the head descending upon the beard, the beard of Aaron. And likewise יִפְרַחַ בְּיָמָיו צַדִּיק — said of King Messiah, in whose days the priesthood returns and the staff of Aaron blossoms."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:30.952355145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}